From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:56:56 -0500
Subject: [RFC PATCH net-next 2/6] ionic: give Tx buffers their own bookkeeping struct

struct ionic_tx_desc_info records the buffers of a Tx descriptor in an
array of struct ionic_buf_info, the struct the Rx path uses for its page
pool buffers. Tx needs only two of its four members: dma_addr and len.
The skb path never writes page and page_offset, and the XDP path writes
them but nothing on the Tx side reads them back.

Add struct ionic_tx_buf_info with just the address and the length, and
use it for the Tx descriptor info. This lets the next patch add per-buffer
unmap state for Tx without growing every Rx buffer, and it shrinks
struct ionic_tx_desc_info by 8 bytes per buffer for now.

No functional change.
